# Development Notes Guidelines

## Technical Documentation Standards

### Code Examples
- Include complete, runnable code snippets
- Add comments to explain complex logic
- Show both basic and advanced use cases
- Include error handling where appropriate
- Use proper syntax highlighting

### Configuration Examples
- Provide complete configuration files
- Include environment-specific variations
- Add explanatory comments
- Show before/after examples when relevant

### Installation and Setup
- Include step-by-step installation instructions
- List prerequisites and dependencies
- Provide troubleshooting guidance
- Include version compatibility notes

### Best Practices
- Document recommended approaches
- Include security considerations
- Add performance tips where relevant
- Provide migration guides for version changes
- Follow the diataxis principle: a section or a file should be clearly categorable in that framework.
